  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative sentiment (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00 with recent lows), as models tend to overreact to short-term volatility.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 15-day average, reduce by 5-10% to align with historical mean reversion patterns.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp spikes: if model predicts >10% above recent peak, cap at 5-7% above prior high to avoid overcorrection.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is neutral (0.00) and true outcome is consistently below forecast — suggest a 3-5% downward adjustment to reflect underestimation risk.",
    "For horizon >30d, apply lag correction: if forecast is 5%+ above true outcome over 3+ days, reduce by 1-2% per day to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "When sentiment history includes 0.50 (positive), slightly increase forecast by 2-3% to reflect bullish momentum, but cap at 10% above prior high to avoid overestimation."
  ]
}
